# P6-90 Integration Report

## Scope and disposition

P6-90 integrates the frozen P6-00, P6-10, and P6-20 contracts through the
MGIF-owned projection, renderer facade, GPU picking/readback, selection,
highlight, clipboard, camera, and host input boundaries. This report is a
candidate engineering integration record. It does not claim Gate P6,
release/distribution approval, Metal verification, or a root-license decision.

The authoritative source state is the final `build/authority-source-manifest.json`
and the two fresh Windows build roots named in `build/machine-identity.json`.
The three frozen read-only paths match their rebind preimages exactly.

## Source changes closed

- Canonical material descriptor layout and renderer-owned sampler are borrowed
  by transaction tables; no incompatible Vulkan descriptor layout is created.
- Transaction vertex/index uploads use explicit `Undefined -> TransferDst ->
  General` buffer barriers.
- Vulkan picking targets are created/retired at frame boundaries and resized
  without recording a stale attachment.
- D3D12 sparse vertex locations use declaration-order fallback after DXIL
  reflection compaction.
- Picking uses a double-sided pipeline so backend Y-flip cannot hide the
  fixture solely through winding.
- `EditorViewportRuntime::coherentPickPublication()` binds fence, occurrence
  generation, projection identity, raw scene epoch, viewport generation, and
  view revision; stale hit/miss/double-focus terminals have zero side effects.
- Host input no longer sends the live `io.MousePos` move into Runtime while a
  native case is active, so delayed samples retain their injected coordinates.
- A native double-focus result is not overwritten by the fixed automation pose
  later in the same frame.
- `RendererFacade::editorPickFence()` exposes the required backend-neutral
  optional fence accessor while retaining the full publication API.

## Windows verification

All authoritative builds used native Windows Visual Studio 2022 MSVC amd64
(19.44.35217.0, toolset 14.38.33130), CMake 4.1.2, and Ninja. WSL was used
only for orchestration and evidence collation.

- Fresh Debug and Release target builds completed successfully.
- Focused CTest completed `33/33` in both configurations, including selection,
  picking, integration, RHI, projection, transaction, Vulkan, D3D12, and
  Android contract tests.
- Debug and Release direct integration/RHI/D3D12 smoke executables returned
  zero.
- SPIR-V validation passed for both generated editor shaders in both
  configurations; six DXIL entrypoints passed Slang/DXC generation and
  dumpbin validation.
- Vulkan CSM production smoke completed 40 frames with empty stderr,
  `stable_recording_budget_met=true`, and zero counted `VUID-` or
  `SYNC-HAZARD` diagnostics.
- D3D12 CSM production smoke completed 40 frames with the same stable budget
  and empty stderr.

## Native interaction matrix

The final Debug and Release Demo binaries each passed the four Vulkan cases:

| Case | Submitted | Terminals | Selection effects | Camera effects | Highlight occurrence |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| `single-hit` | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 1 |
| `same-primitive-toggle` | 2 | 2 | 2 | 0 | 1 |
| `blank-clear` | 2 | 2 | 2 | 0 | 1 |
| `double-focus` | 1 | 1 | 0 | 1 | 0 |

Every case reported `completed=true`; the final view/selection revisions
match the expected single-effect transitions. The window-cropped PNG is
non-empty (`1936x1119`, non-zero mean and standard deviation) and visibly
contains the Scene Browser, Inspector primitive context, and selection
outline.

## Explicit limitations

The current Windows adapter reports the combined `r32Uint`/`d32` sampled
attachment capability as unsupported for D3D12 (`formats=0`). Accordingly,
the D3D12 native-picking case is recorded as **BLOCKED**, not PASS. D3D12
public/RHI contracts and production CSM smoke still pass. Metal has no
macOS artifact and remains **Not Verified / not_run**. F42/R24 and
release/distribution remain blocked by the locked license policy.

